.TITLE "ping"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Verifies IP-level connectivity to another TCP/IP computer by sending ICMP Echo Request messages. It measures the __round-trip time__ and reports packet loss.

.DIV "ALIAS"

.DIV "TLDR"
**ping hostname**
Sends echo requests to the specified hostname or IP address.
> __hostname__ the target destination

**ping -t hostname**
Pings the specified host continuously until interrupted.
> __-t__ continuous flag

**ping -n 10 hostname**
Sends a specific number of echo requests.
> __-n 10__ count flag

**ping -l 1000 hostname**
Sends echo requests with a specific buffer size in bytes.
> __-l 1000__ buffer size flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Using __ping__ is the first step in troubleshooting network connectivity issues. A successful ping indicates that the basic network path between the two devices is functional.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**windows:tracert** **windows:ipconfig**

